            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-52616",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "avahi: Avahi Wide-Area DNS Predictable Transaction IDs"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in the Avahi-daemon, where it initializes DNS transaction IDs randomly only once at startup, incrementing them sequentially after that. This predictable behavior facilitates DNS spoofing attacks, allowing attackers to guess transaction IDs."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-52616",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-52616\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: libavahi-core7\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2024-52616](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-52616)\nA flaw was found in the Avahi-daemon, where it initializes DNS transaction IDs randomly only once at startup, incrementing them sequentially after that. This predictable behavior facilitates DNS spoofing attacks, allowing attackers to guess transaction IDs.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-52616**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|libavahi-core7||[CVE-2024-52616](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-52616)|\n\nA flaw was found in the Avahi-daemon, where it initializes DNS transaction IDs randomly only once at startup, incrementing them sequentially after that. This predictable behavior facilitates DNS spoofing attacks, allowing attackers to guess transaction IDs."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-5278",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "coreutils: Heap Buffer Under-Read in GNU Coreutils sort via Key Specification"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in GNU Coreutils. The sort utility's begfield() function is vulnerable to a heap buffer under-read. The program may access memory outside the allocated buffer if a user runs a crafted command using the traditional key format. A malicious input could lead to a crash or leak sensitive data."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-5278",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-5278\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: coreutils\nFixed Version: 9.4-3ubuntu6.3\nLink: [CVE-2025-5278](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-5278)\nA flaw was found in GNU Coreutils. The sort utility's begfield() function is vulnerable to a heap buffer under-read. The program may access memory outside the allocated buffer if a user runs a crafted command using the traditional key format. A malicious input could lead to a crash or leak sensitive data.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-5278**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|coreutils|9.4-3ubuntu6.3|[CVE-2025-5278](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-5278)|\n\nA flaw was found in GNU Coreutils. The sort utility's begfield() function is vulnerable to a heap buffer under-read. The program may access memory outside the allocated buffer if a user runs a crafted command using the traditional key format. A malicious input could lead to a crash or leak sensitive data."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
