            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-39821",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "golang.org/x/net/idna: golang: net/http: golang.org/x/net/idna: Privilege escalation via incorrect Punycode label processing"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The ToASCII and ToUnicode functions incorrectly accept Punycode-encoded labels that decode to an ASCII-only label. For example, ToUnicode(\"xn--example-.com\") incorrectly returns the name \"example.com\" rather than an error. This behavior can lead to privilege escalation in programs using the idna package. For example, a program which performs privilege checks on the ASCII hostname may reject \"example.com\" but permit \"xn--example-.com\". If that program subsequently converts the ASCII hostname to Unicode, it will inadvertently permits access to the Unicode name \"example.com\"."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39821",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-39821\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.25.13, 1.26.6, 1.27.0-rc.3\nLink: [CVE-2026-39821](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39821)\nThe ToASCII and ToUnicode functions incorrectly accept Punycode-encoded labels that decode to an ASCII-only label. For example, ToUnicode(\"xn--example-.com\") incorrectly returns the name \"example.com\" rather than an error. This behavior can lead to privilege escalation in programs using the idna package. For example, a program which performs privilege checks on the ASCII hostname may reject \"example.com\" but permit \"xn--example-.com\". If that program subsequently converts the ASCII hostname to Unicode, it will inadvertently permits access to the Unicode name \"example.com\".",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-39821**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|stdlib|1.25.13, 1.26.6, 1.27.0-rc.3|[CVE-2026-39821](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39821)|\n\nThe ToASCII and ToUnicode functions incorrectly accept Punycode-encoded labels that decode to an ASCII-only label. For example, ToUnicode(\"xn--example-.com\") incorrectly returns the name \"example.com\" rather than an error. This behavior can lead to privilege escalation in programs using the idna package. For example, a program which performs privilege checks on the ASCII hostname may reject \"example.com\" but permit \"xn--example-.com\". If that program subsequently converts the ASCII hostname to Unicode, it will inadvertently permits access to the Unicode name \"example.com\"."
